From a2e07f709987604649fd01932245687aa41ad5c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObliviOS Build <build@oblivios.local>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:40:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: add the domains of the Compartments exit service

The exit daemon (exitd), the route helper (exitd_route, the same binary with --routes) and the exit app (exit_app) of ADR-184
and ADR-186.

exitd creates the tun interface (TUNSETIFF and TUNGETIFF only), finds the owner uid of a flow with sock_diag, has ordinary tcp
and udp sockets and keeps the Tor state under /data/misc/exitd. It has no NETLINK_ROUTE write and no netfilter socket; a
neverallow keeps it so.

exitd_route has one NETLINK_ROUTE socket with net_admin and the nlmsg types of the closed rule language (rules, routes, the
tun address and link), and no inet socket of any kind. It transitions from init through domain_trans only: its service
definition names its label, and the type_transition of the daemon stays the default for exitd_exec.

exit_app is a platform-signed privileged app domain like logviewer_app. It connects to the two sockets of init; a neverallow
lets no other domain connect to them. The socket modes in the init definition are the only discretionary control, the peer
check of the services reads the SELinux context of the connecting socket.

No neverallow of the tree is changed.
